# Backtick names with `\` or quotes get a quoted name that lexes back to the same name.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | project `a\b`, `it's "x"`
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..30
  PIPELINE@0..29
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    PROJECT_OP@4..11
      IDENT@4..11 "project"
    WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
    ERROR@12..29
      ERROR@12..17 "`a\\b`"
      COMMA@17..18 ","
      WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
      ERROR@19..29 "`it's \"x\"`"
  WHITESPACE@29..30 "\n"

error[DS0001]: names are not quoted with backticks
  --> query:1:13
  |
1 | t | project `a\b`, `it's "x"`
  |             ^^^^^ backticks are not a quote
  |
  = help: quote the name with brackets: `['a\\b']`

error[DS0001]: names are not quoted with backticks
  --> query:1:20
  |
1 | t | project `a\b`, `it's "x"`
  |                    ^^^^^^^^^^ backticks are not a quote
  |
  = help: quote the name with brackets: `['it\'s "x"']`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    t | project ['a\\b'], ['it\'s "x"']
which parses without errors
